   'Hall honors U.S. Air Force Capt. Ryan P. Hall, 30, of Colorado Springs, Colorado, who was assigned to the 319th Special Operations Squadron at Hurlburt Field, Florida. He died on Feb. 18, 2012, when his single-engine U-28 aircraft crashed near Camp Lemonnier, Djibouti.

You complete 5 rounds of 3 cleans (225 lb / 155 lb), a 200 m sprint and 20 kettlebell snatches (53 lb / 35 lb), 10 on each arm. You rest 2 minutes between rounds. The rest lets you go hard on every round, so the heavy cleans come with a racing heart from the sprint before. CrossFit does not say whether the rest counts in your time, so choose one and note it with your score.',
   '[{"name": "Cleans", "reps": "3", "tip": "Heavy for most people. Take each rep as a single and catch it in a power or squat position.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "155 lb"}, {"name": "Sprint", "reps": "200 m", "tip": "A real sprint. You get to rest after the snatches."}, {"name": "Kettlebell Snatches", "reps": "20 (10 each arm)", "tip": "Punch through at the top so the bell does not crash on your wrist. Switch arms at 10.", "rx_men": "53 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Rest", "reps": "2 min", "isRest": true, "tip": "Rest between rounds. There is no rest after the fifth round."}]'::jsonb,
