   'Lower the cleans to 135 lb / 95 lb or less, a load you can clean safely after a sprint. Use a lighter kettlebell, or do dumbbell snatches. Shorten the sprint to 100 m if running fast is new for you. The 2-minute rest stays, so you can still push each round.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Hall workout?", "answer": "5 rounds for time of 3 cleans (225 lb / 155 lb), a 200 m sprint and 20 kettlebell snatches (53 lb / 35 lb), 10 each arm, with 2 minutes of rest between rounds."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Hall?", "answer": "15 cleans, 100 kettlebell snatches and 1,000 m of sprinting, with 4 rest periods of 2 minutes."}, {"question": "Who was Hall?", "answer": "U.S. Air Force Capt. Ryan P. Hall, 30, of the 319th Special Operations Squadron. He died on Feb. 18, 2012, when his U-28 aircraft crashed near Camp Lemonnier, Djibouti."}, {"question": "Does the rest count in my time?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Many athletes run one clock and include the rest, but either way works if you note which you chose."}]'::jsonb,
