   'Hamilton honors U.S. Army Spc. Adam Hamilton, 22, of Kent, Ohio, who served with the 4th Squadron, 4th Cavalry Regiment, 1st Infantry Division, based at Fort Riley, Kansas. He died on May 28, 2011, in Haji Ruf, Afghanistan, of wounds from an improvised explosive device attack on his unit.

You complete 3 rounds of a 1,000 m row, 50 push-ups, a 1,000 m run and 50 pull-ups. That is 3,000 m of rowing, 3,000 m of running, 150 push-ups and 150 pull-ups. The long row and run give your arms a break, but the push-up and pull-up totals add up quickly, so your sets get shorter each round.',
   '[{"name": "Row", "reps": "1,000 m", "tip": "Hold a steady pace. Push with your legs first, then pull with your arms."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "50", "tip": "Chest to the floor and lock out at the top. Break into sets of 10 or so from the start."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "1,000 m", "tip": "Settle into a pace you can repeat on all 3 rounds."}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "50", "tip": "Chin over the bar on every rep. Small sets keep your grip fresh."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Pace the first round like the last", "Break the push-ups and pull-ups early", "Use the row and run to recover your arms"]'::jsonb,
   '["Pick a rowing pace you could hold for twice the distance, so you get off the rower with legs left.", "Split the 50 push-ups into planned sets, such as 5 sets of 10, before your arms fail.", "Shake out your arms and grip during the first few hundred meters of the run.", "Kip or do strict pull-ups, but keep the sets small, such as 5 to 10 reps, with short rests.", "Chalk your hands before each set of pull-ups."]'::jsonb,
   'Cut the row and run to 500 m each, or do 2 rounds instead of 3. Do push-ups from your knees or with your hands on a box. Use a band for pull-ups, or replace them with ring rows. Lowering the reps to 25 push-ups and 25 pull-ups per round keeps the same idea with less volume.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Hamilton workout?", "answer": "3 rounds for time of a 1,000 m row, 50 push-ups, a 1,000 m run and 50 pull-ups."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Hamilton?", "answer": "150 push-ups and 150 pull-ups, plus 3,000 m of rowing and 3,000 m of running."}, {"question": "Who was Hamilton?", "answer": "U.S. Army Spc. Adam Hamilton, 22, of Kent, Ohio, of the 1st Infantry Division. He died on May 28, 2011, in Haji Ruf, Afghanistan, of wounds from an improvised explosive device attack."}, {"question": "Can I kip the pull-ups?", "answer": "Yes. CrossFit does not ask for strict pull-ups in Hamilton, so any pull-up where your chin clears the bar counts."}]'::jsonb,
