   'time',
   'Hammy honors Cpl Stuart "Hammy" Hamilton, 30, of the 2nd Battalion, Royal Irish Regiment, who died on Sept. 4, 2021, in a training accident. A military reservist and Afghanistan veteran, he was an avid athlete who once ran a half marathon in a 60 lb vest.

This is a long chipper that runs to a middle point and back. You run 1,200 m, 800 m, 400 m, 400 m, 800 m and 1,200 m, with box step-overs (24 in / 20 in), hand-release push-ups, burpees to a target, strict pull-ups, burpee box jumps and 10 ring muscle-ups in between. The second half repeats the first in reverse, so pace the opening run and the 80 step-overs with that in mind.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "1,200 m", "tip": "Start easy. There are 4,800 m of running in total."}, {"name": "Box Step-Overs", "reps": "80", "tip": "Step up, stand tall on the box and step down the other side.", "rx_men": "24 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Hand-Release Push-Ups", "reps": "40", "tip": "Lift your hands off the floor at the bottom of every rep."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Steady pace. Shake out your arms."}, {"name": "Burpees (to a 6-inch target)", "reps": "40", "tip": "Jump and touch a target set 6 in above your reach on every rep."}, {"name": "Strict Pull-Ups", "reps": "20", "tip": "No kip. Start from a dead hang and pull until your chin clears the bar."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "A short run before the hardest skill work."}, {"name": "Burpee Box Jumps", "reps": "20", "tip": "Burpee, then jump onto the box. CrossFit does not say whether to step down or jump over.", "rx_men": "24 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Ring Muscle-Ups", "reps": "10", "tip": "Quick singles with a short rest are fine."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Halfway. The work now repeats in reverse."}, {"name": "Burpees (to a 6-inch target)", "reps": "40", "tip": "Same target as before. Keep a steady rhythm."}, {"name": "Strict Pull-Ups", "reps": "20", "tip": "Small sets from a dead hang."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Hold your pace."}, {"name": "Box Step-Overs", "reps": "80", "tip": "Steady steps. Switch your lead leg often.", "rx_men": "24 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Hand-Release Push-Ups", "reps": "40", "tip": "Short sets before your arms fail."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "1,200 m", "tip": "The last effort. Push the pace."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Start the first run slower than you want to", "Break the strict pull-ups into small sets", "Remember the second half mirrors the first"]'::jsonb,
   '["Switch your lead leg on the box step-overs to share the load between both legs.", "On the hand-release push-ups, keep your body straight and press the whole body up together.", "CrossFit lists a 6 in target for the burpees. The usual setup is a target 6 in above your standing reach, so set it before you start.", "Do the strict pull-ups in sets of 3 to 5 from the start, before your grip fades.", "Take the ring muscle-ups as singles with a short rest if you need to, and do not waste energy on failed reps."]'::jsonb,
   'Use a lower box, shorten the runs by half, or cut the reps in half. Do push-ups from your knees, burpees without the target, and banded or jumping pull-ups. Replace the ring muscle-ups with 20 ring rows and 20 ring dips, or 10 jumping muscle-ups from a low ring.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Hammy workout?", "answer": "For time: 1,200 m run, 80 box step-overs, 40 hand-release push-ups, 800 m run, 40 burpees to target, 20 strict pull-ups, 400 m run, 20 burpee box jumps, 10 ring muscle-ups, 400 m run, 40 burpees to target, 20 strict pull-ups, 800 m run, 80 box step-overs, 40 hand-release push-ups, 1,200 m run. The box is 24 in / 20 in."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Hammy?", "answer": "160 box step-overs, 80 hand-release push-ups, 80 burpees to target, 40 strict pull-ups, 20 burpee box jumps and 10 ring muscle-ups, plus 4,800 m of running."}, {"question": "Who was Hammy?", "answer": "Cpl Stuart \"Hammy\" Hamilton, 30, of the 2nd Battalion, Royal Irish Regiment. The reservist and Afghanistan veteran died on Sept. 4, 2021, in a training accident."}, {"question": "What does a 6-inch target for burpees mean?", "answer": "CrossFit lists a 6 in target and does not explain it further. The usual setup is a target 6 in above your standing reach that you touch at the top of each burpee."}]'::jsonb,
