   'Harper honors Phoenix Firefighter Brad Harper, 23, of Peoria, Arizona, who was assigned to Rescue 21 and had served with the Phoenix Fire Department for two years. He died on the scene of a two-alarm fire on May 19, 2013.

You have 23 minutes to complete as many rounds as you can of 9 chest-to-bar pull-ups, 15 power cleans (135 lb / 95 lb), 21 squats and a 400 m run carrying a plate (45 lb / 25 lb). The plate run is the longest piece of each round and tires your arms and grip, right before you go back to the pull-up bar.',
   '[{"name": "Chest-to-Bar Pull-Ups", "reps": "9", "tip": "Your chest must touch the bar on every rep. Small sets keep you moving."}, {"name": "Power Cleans", "reps": "15", "tip": "Quick touch-and-go sets or fast singles. Keep the bar close.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Air Squats", "reps": "21", "tip": "Hips below the knees and stand all the way up."}, {"name": "Run with Plate", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Hold the plate at your chest or on your shoulders, and switch when your arms tire.", "rx_men": "45 lb plate", "rx_women": "25 lb plate"}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total rounds + reps.',
   '["Break the power cleans before you need to", "Find a plate grip you can hold for 400 m", "Keep the squats moving"]'::jsonb,
   '["Split the 15 power cleans into sets you can repeat every round, such as 3 sets of 5.", "On the chest-to-bar pull-ups, kip with your hips and pull your chest to the bar, not just your chin over it.", "Set the plate next to your barbell so you can grab it and go after the squats.", "Hold the plate close to your chest and keep your stride short and quick.", "Count a round as finished when you drop the plate back at the start."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the power cleans to 95 lb / 65 lb or less, and use a lighter plate or run without one. Replace chest-to-bar pull-ups with regular pull-ups, banded pull-ups or ring rows. Cut the run to 200 m if you want more rounds of barbell and bar work.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Harper workout?", "answer": "As many rounds as possible in 23 minutes of 9 chest-to-bar pull-ups, 15 power cleans (135 lb / 95 lb), 21 squats and a 400 m run with a plate (45 lb / 25 lb)."}, {"question": "How many reps are in one round of Harper?", "answer": "45 reps (9 chest-to-bar pull-ups, 15 power cleans and 21 squats), plus the 400 m plate run."}, {"question": "Who was Harper?", "answer": "Phoenix Firefighter Brad Harper, 23, of Peoria, Arizona, of Rescue 21. He died on the scene of a two-alarm fire on May 19, 2013."}, {"question": "How do I carry the plate on the run?", "answer": "CrossFit does not set a carry style. Hold it at your chest, on your shoulder or overhead, and switch when your arms tire."}]'::jsonb,
