   'Do 150 single-unders, or 50–75 double-unders, instead of 150 double-unders. Do push-ups from your knees or with your hands on a box. Lower the power cleans to 135 lb / 95 lb or less, a load you can move in fast singles.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Havana workout?", "answer": "As many rounds as possible in 25 minutes of 150 double-unders, 50 push-ups and 15 power cleans (185 lb / 125 lb)."}, {"question": "How many reps are in one round of Havana?", "answer": "215 reps: 150 double-unders, 50 push-ups and 15 power cleans."}, {"question": "Who was Havana?", "answer": "Italian Army C.le Magg. Sc. Roberto Marchini, 28, of Viterbo, Italy, of the 8th Airborne Combat Engineer Regiment, Folgore Brigade. He died on July 12, 2011, during a reconnaissance mission in Afghanistan''s Bakwa district."}, {"question": "Why these three movements?", "answer": "CrossFit notes that double-unders, push-ups and power cleans were Marchini''s favorite exercises."}]'::jsonb,
