You complete a 100-calorie row, 75 thrusters (45 lb / 35 lb), 50 pull-ups, 75 wall balls (20 lb to 10 ft / 14 lb to 9 ft) and a second 100-calorie row. CrossFit lists a weight vest (20 lb / 14 lb) with the loads. The barbell is light, but 200 calories of rowing and 150 squatting reps make this a long test of pacing.',
   '[{"name": "Row for Calories", "reps": "100 cal", "tip": "Steady pace. You have another 100 calories to row at the end."}, {"name": "Thrusters", "reps": "75", "tip": "Front squat, then drive the bar straight overhead in one move.", "rx_men": "45 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "50", "tip": "Chin over the bar on every rep. Small sets with the vest on."}, {"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "75", "tip": "Full squat and hit the target every rep. Break into planned sets.", "rx_men": "20 lb to 10 ft", "rx_women": "14 lb to 9 ft"}, {"name": "Row for Calories", "reps": "100 cal", "tip": "The last effort. Build the pace over the final 25 calories."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
