   'Hollywood honors Sgt. Jonathan Stuart "Hollywood" Hollingsworth, 35, of Rotherham, Yorkshire, England, who served with D Squadron, 22nd SAS Regiment, in the British Army. He was killed on Nov. 23, 2006, during a mission in Basra, Iraq. He received the Conspicuous Gallantry Cross and the Queen''s Gallantry Medal, and he loved running, skydiving and rugby.

You run 2,000 m, then complete 22 wall balls, 22 muscle-ups, 22 wall balls, 22 power cleans (185 lb / 125 lb) and 22 more wall balls, and finish with another 2,000 m run. The wall ball is heavy at 30 lb to 10 ft / 20 lb to 9 ft, and the muscle-ups and cleans come between sets that tire your legs and shoulders.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "2,000 m", "tip": "Steady pace. Save something for the barbell and rings."}, {"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "22", "tip": "A heavy ball. Full squat and use your legs to drive it to the target.", "rx_men": "30 lb to 10 ft", "rx_women": "20 lb to 9 ft"}, {"name": "Muscle-Ups", "reps": "22", "tip": "Ring muscle-ups. Quick singles or small sets."}, {"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "22", "tip": "Short sets with short rests.", "rx_men": "30 lb to 10 ft", "rx_women": "20 lb to 9 ft"}, {"name": "Power Cleans", "reps": "22", "tip": "Heavy for most people. Fast singles with a flat back.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "22", "tip": "The last set before the final run.", "rx_men": "30 lb to 10 ft", "rx_women": "20 lb to 9 ft"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "2,000 m", "tip": "The last effort. Build the pace over the final 500 m."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
