   '[{"question": "What is the Hollywood workout?", "answer": "For time: 2,000 m run, 22 wall balls, 22 muscle-ups, 22 wall balls, 22 power cleans (185 lb / 125 lb), 22 wall balls, 2,000 m run. The wall ball is 30 lb to 10 ft / 20 lb to 9 ft."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Hollywood?", "answer": "66 wall balls, 22 muscle-ups and 22 power cleans, plus 4,000 m of running."}, {"question": "Who was Hollywood?", "answer": "Sgt. Jonathan Stuart \"Hollywood\" Hollingsworth, 35, of Rotherham, England, of D Squadron, 22nd SAS Regiment. He was killed on Nov. 23, 2006, during a mission in Basra, Iraq."}, {"question": "Are the muscle-ups on rings or a bar?", "answer": "CrossFit writes muscle-ups without saying rings or bar. Ring muscle-ups are the usual standard, and you can note it if you use a bar."}]'::jsonb,
