   'time',
   'Horton honors U.S. Army Spc. Christopher D. Horton, 26, of Collinsville, Oklahoma, who was assigned to the 1st Battalion, 279th Infantry Regiment, 45th Infantry Brigade Combat Team, Oklahoma National Guard. He died on Sept. 9, 2011, in Zurmat District, Afghanistan, of wounds from a small-arms fire attack on his unit.

This is a partner workout. Your team completes 9 rounds of 9 bar muscle-ups, 11 clean and jerks (155 lb / 105 lb) and a 50 yd buddy carry. Share the work however you choose, with one person working at a time. Without a partner, do 5 reps of each exercise per round and carry a heavy sandbag. The buddy carry means the stronger partner often carries more.',
   '[{"name": "Bar Muscle-Up", "reps": "9", "tip": "Shared between partners. Quick singles or small sets."}, {"name": "Clean and Jerks", "reps": "11", "tip": "Shared between partners. Clean to your shoulders, then jerk to lockout.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}, {"name": "Buddy Carry", "reps": "50 yd", "tip": "One partner carries the other. Solo, carry a heavy sandbag instead.", "rx_men": "Partner or heavy sandbag", "rx_women": "Partner or heavy sandbag"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Agree on how you will split the reps before you start", "Switch often so both partners stay fresh", "Pick a carry style you can hold for 50 yd"]'::jsonb,
   '["One person works at a time, so short, fast sets with quick changes keep the clock moving.", "On the bar muscle-ups, kip your hips to the bar and press to lockout at the top.", "Drop the barbell from the top under control and reset your grip before the next rep.", "For the buddy carry, a fireman''s carry or piggyback both work. CrossFit does not set a style, so use what is safe for your pair.", "Solo athletes should pick a sandbag that is heavy but lets them finish 50 yd without dropping it more than once."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the clean and jerks to 115 lb / 75 lb or less. Replace bar muscle-ups with chest-to-bar or regular pull-ups, at about 2 pull-ups for each muscle-up. Swap the buddy carry for a sandbag carry if a partner carry is not safe for your pair. Solo, follow CrossFit''s version of 5 reps of each exercise per round with a heavy sandbag.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Horton workout?", "answer": "9 rounds for time, with a partner, of 9 bar muscle-ups, 11 clean and jerks (155 lb / 105 lb) and a 50 yd buddy carry. One partner works at a time, and you split the work however you choose."}, {"question": "Can I do Horton without a partner?", "answer": "Yes. CrossFit says to do 5 reps of each exercise per round and carry a heavy sandbag 50 yd instead of a partner."}, {"question": "Who was Horton?", "answer": "U.S. Army Spc. Christopher D. Horton, 26, of Collinsville, Oklahoma, of the Oklahoma National Guard. He died on Sept. 9, 2011, in Zurmat District, Afghanistan, of wounds from a small-arms fire attack."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Horton?", "answer": "With a partner, the team completes 81 bar muscle-ups, 99 clean and jerks and 450 yd of buddy carries. Solo, it is 45 bar muscle-ups, 45 clean and jerks and 450 yd of sandbag carries."}]'::jsonb,
