   'Lower the squat cleans to 135 lb / 95 lb or less. Do handstand push-ups from the floor, with an abmat under your head, or as pike push-ups with your feet on a box. You can also cut the ladder to 1–5 and 5–1.',
   '[{"question": "What is the J.J. workout?", "answer": "For time: squat cleans (185 lb / 125 lb) that climb from 1 to 10 reps, alternating with parallette handstand push-ups that drop from 10 to 1. Start with 1 squat clean and 10 handstand push-ups."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in J.J.?", "answer": "55 squat cleans and 55 parallette handstand push-ups."}, {"question": "Who was J.J.?", "answer": "U.S. Marine Lance Cpl. Justin James \"JJ\" Wilson, 24, of Palm City, Florida, of the 2nd Marine Division. He was killed on March 22, 2010, while supporting combat operations in Helmand Province, Afghanistan."}, {"question": "What if I do not have parallettes?", "answer": "Use two stacks of plates or sturdy boxes for a deficit, or do the handstand push-ups from the floor and note it with your time."}]'::jsonb,
