   'This workout honors Chief Warrant Officer 2 Jonathan Farmer, 37, of Boynton Beach, Florida, a U.S. Army Special Forces soldier with the 5th Special Forces Group (Airborne). He served on seven overseas combat tours and died on Jan. 16, 2019, of wounds from an attack while conducting a local engagement in Manbij, Syria. CrossFit spells the workout''s name "Jonathon."

You row 1,500 m, then complete 2 rounds of 53 push-ups, 11 pull-ups, 5 shoulder presses (135 lb / 95 lb), a 100 m farmers carry (70 lb / 35 lb), a 50 m sled push (90 lb / 45 lb) and a 300 m sprint. You finish with another 1,500 m row. You need a sled and farmers carry handles, dumbbells or kettlebells.',
   '[{"name": "Row", "reps": "1,500 m", "tip": "Hold a pace you could keep for twice the distance."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "53", "tip": "Chest to the floor and full lockout. Break into sets of 10 or so from the start."}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "11", "tip": "Chin over the bar on every rep."}, {"name": "Overhead Press", "reps": "5", "tip": "Strict shoulder press. No dip or leg drive.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Farmers Carry", "reps": "100 m", "tip": "Stand tall, shoulders back, and walk with short, quick steps.", "rx_men": "70 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Sled Push", "reps": "50 m", "tip": "Arms straight, body low, and drive with your legs.", "rx_men": "90 lb", "rx_women": "45 lb"}, {"name": "Sprint", "reps": "300 m", "tip": "Fast, but keep enough to start the next round."}, {"name": "Row", "reps": "1,500 m", "tip": "The last effort. Build the pace over the final 500 m."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
