   'Cut each row to 1,000 m. Do push-ups from your knees or with your hands on a box, and use a band or ring rows for the pull-ups. Lower the shoulder press to 95 lb / 65 lb or less. Use lighter farmers carry weights and a lighter sled. With no sled, do a 50 m heavy sandbag or plate drag instead, knowing this changes the workout.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Jonathon Farmer workout?", "answer": "For time: 1,500 m row, then 2 rounds of 53 push-ups, 11 pull-ups, 5 shoulder presses (135 lb / 95 lb), 100 m farmers carry (70 lb / 35 lb), 50 m sled push (90 lb / 45 lb) and 300 m sprint, then a 1,500 m row."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Jonathon Farmer?", "answer": "106 push-ups, 22 pull-ups and 10 shoulder presses, plus 3,000 m of rowing, 200 m of farmers carry, 100 m of sled push and 600 m of sprinting."}, {"question": "Who was Jonathan Farmer?", "answer": "Chief Warrant Officer 2 Jonathan Farmer, 37, of Boynton Beach, Florida, of the 5th Special Forces Group (Airborne). He died on Jan. 16, 2019, of wounds from an attack in Manbij, Syria. CrossFit spells the workout name \"Jonathon.\""}, {"question": "Is the farmers carry weight per hand?", "answer": "CrossFit lists 70 lb / 35 lb and does not say. Per hand is the more common reading, but note what you used with your time."}]'::jsonb,
